From 58eebf4dd62a37e001e99dbe3f36b15f6c716af1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joe214214 <y852zhou@uwaterloo.ca>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:37:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(read_video): rank scene changes instead of
 thresholding them

ffmpeg scene scores depend on content: film cuts score above 0.3, but an
error banner in a screen recording scored 0.13 and a text edit ~0.005, so
the 0.3 threshold returned only the first frame of UI recordings. Score
every frame on a 320 px copy, keep the first frame plus the highest-scoring
changes spaced at least minFrameGapSeconds apart, and extract each by seek.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HKCB8j9Zf27m5tAmJdbkFm
